§ `Part V - Termination of residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 4 - Orders for termination of residential tenancy agreement`

§§§ `76A. Termination of agreement by lessor if premises abandoned`

DECLARE `abandonment notice` HAS
    `the lessor suspects on reasonable grounds that the tenant has abandoned the residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is signed by or for the lessor or property manager` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice identifies the residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the lessor is terminating the agreement because the tenant has abandoned the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the tenant was given the notice` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant has taken action under section 76B to dispute the notice` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.76A
@export Decide whether a lessor's abandonment notice under s.76A is in the required form
GIVEN n IS A `abandonment notice` @desc The lessor suspects on reasonable grounds that the tenant has abandoned the premises. The notice must be written, in the approved form, signed by or for the lessor or property manager, identify the premises, and state that the lessor is terminating because the tenant has abandoned the premises.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abandonment notice is in the required form` IF
        n's `the lessor suspects on reasonable grounds that the tenant has abandoned the residential premises`
    AND n's `the notice is in writing`
    AND n's `the notice is in the approved form`
    AND n's `the notice is signed by or for the lessor or property manager`
    AND n's `the notice identifies the residential premises`
    AND n's `the notice states the lessor is terminating the agreement because the tenant has abandoned the premises`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.76A(3)
@export Decide whether the tenant is taken to have abandoned the premises under s.76A(3)
GIVEN n IS A `abandonment notice` @desc If the tenant does not take action under s.76B within 7 days after being given a s.76A notice in the required form, the tenant is taken to have abandoned the premises.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is taken to have abandoned the premises` IF
        `the abandonment notice is in the required form` n
    AND NOT n's `the tenant has taken action under section 76B to dispute the notice`
    AND n's `days after the tenant was given the notice` GREATER THAN 7

§§§ `76B. Dispute about s. 76A notice`

DECLARE `section 76B application` HAS
    `days after the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant wishes to dispute a notice given under section 76A` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.76B
@export Decide whether the tenant may apply to dispute a s.76A notice
GIVEN a IS A `section 76B application` @desc The tenant may apply within 28 days after the notice is given. If the application is made within 7 days, the court may set the notice aside.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may apply to dispute the abandonment notice` IF
        a's `the tenant wishes to dispute a notice given under section 76A`
    AND a's `days after the notice was given` AT MOST 28
    AND a's `days after the notice was given` AT LEAST 0

GIVEN a IS A `section 76B application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order setting aside the notice` IF
        `the tenant may apply to dispute the abandonment notice` a
    AND a's `days after the notice was given` AT MOST 7

§§ `Fixtures`

`valid abandonment notice not disputed` MEANS `abandonment notice` WITH
    `the lessor suspects on reasonable grounds that the tenant has abandoned the residential premises` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in writing` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is signed by or for the lessor or property manager` IS TRUE,
    `the notice identifies the residential premises` IS TRUE,
    `the notice states the lessor is terminating the agreement because the tenant has abandoned the premises` IS TRUE,
    `days after the tenant was given the notice` IS 8,
    `the tenant has taken action under section 76B to dispute the notice` IS FALSE

`abandonment disputed on day 5` MEANS `section 76B application` WITH
    `days after the notice was given` IS 5,
    `the tenant wishes to dispute a notice given under section 76A` IS TRUE

`abandonment disputed on day 30` MEANS `section 76B application` WITH
    `days after the notice was given` IS 30,
    `the tenant wishes to dispute a notice given under section 76A` IS TRUE

#EVAL `the tenant is taken to have abandoned the premises` `valid abandonment notice not disputed`
#EVAL `the court may make an order setting aside the notice` `abandonment disputed on day 5`
#EVAL `the tenant may apply to dispute the abandonment notice` `abandonment disputed on day 30`
#ASSERT `the tenant is taken to have abandoned the premises` `valid abandonment notice not disputed` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may make an order setting aside the notice` `abandonment disputed on day 5` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant may apply to dispute the abandonment notice` `abandonment disputed on day 30` EQUALS FALSE
